c86beb5ef657a19af9f510c07091.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 27 at 11:20AM MDT until August 27 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-27T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9798323cad440114383a15e74c30c9e9a07095b8.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9798323cad440114383a15e74c30c9e9a07095b8.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-27T23:29:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 272329 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 529 PM MDT Thu Aug 27 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and storms into tonight. Flash flooding possible for the Aspen Acres burn scar, with a few severe storms possible along I-25. - Daily showers and storms will continue over the mountains each day into next week. The eastern plains will be a bit warmer and m","url":"https://forecast.weathe